          "body": "A few docs links point at heading ids that don't exist on h3.dev, so they open the page but don't jump to the section:\n\n- basics/middleware: `lifecycle#\\_3-dispatch-request` → `#3-dispatch-request` (the escaped underscore ends up in the href)\n- basics/response: `h3event#eventres` → `#h3eventres`\n- api/h3event: `request#getrouterparamsevent-opts-decode` → `#getrouterparamsevent-opts--decode-`, and `security#resolvedotsegments` → `#resolvedotsegmentspath-opts` (these are the ids automd generates from the signatures)\n\nI checked every new fragment against the live ids on h3.dev.\n\nNot fixed here: routing.md links `removeRoute` to `/utils/more#removerouteapp-method-route`, but `src/utils/route.ts` (`defineRoute` / `removeRoute`) isn't in any automd block, so that section doesn't exist. Adding a `<!-- automd:jsdocs src=\"../../src/utils/route.ts\" -->` block would cover it. I left that for you to decide.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated several guide links to point to the correct sections for request dispatch, response APIs, and pathname encoding.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
