          },
          "body": "An SSE message with `id: \"\"` must send an empty `id` field so an EventSource client can clear its last event ID. The current truthiness check drops that field, leaving the previous reconnection cursor in effect. The [HTML SSE specification](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html#parsing-an-event-stream) defines an empty `id` value as resetting the last event ID.\n\nCheck whether the optional ID is a string so empty IDs are emitted and omitted IDs remain omitted. Wire-format regressions cover both a single message and an empty ID following a non-empty ID in a batch.\n\nValidation on Node 24.21.0:\n- Both new wire-format cases fail before the fix; all 53 SSE unit and integration tests pass after it.\n- Lint, formatting, typecheck and `pnpm build` pass.\n- The full unmodified test fixture run reports only the existing loopback IP expectation failure (`::ffff:127.0.0.1`); 3,037 tests pass, 51 skip after `pnpm build` (matching the CI build/test order). Applying the independent loopback test expectation locally allows the full suite to pass (3,038 passed, 51 skipped); that test-only change is excluded from this PR.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Empty event IDs are now included in formatted event stream messages, both individually and in batches. IDs continue to have newline characters removed.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Clarified that an empty event ID resets the client’s last event ID, while omitting the ID leaves it unchanged.\n  * Added documentation explaining that event stream comments are terminated by a blank line.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
